Reflect  $I$  over  $M$ . Let that point be  $I_A$ , which is the  $A-\text{Excenter}$ . Let  $T$  be the midpoint of  $\widehat{BAC}$ . Now by a  $\sqrt{AB\cdot AC}$  Inversion followed by a reflection along the angle bisector of  $\angle BAC (\Psi)$ , we get that  $AK$  is the  $A-\text{Symmedian}$  of  $\triangle ABC$ . So,  $-1=(AK;BC)\overset{M}{=}(DS;BC)$ . So,  $AS$  is the  $A-$  External bisector of  $\angle BAC$ . So,  $\overline{S-A-T}$ . Now consider the  $\triangle STI_A$ . Notice that  $\odot(AMN)$  is the Nine-Point Circle of  $\triangle STI_A$  and  $I$  is the orthocenter. Let  $L_1$  be the foot of altitude from  $T$  onto  $SI_A$ . So,  $L_1\in\odot(AMN)$  and if  $P$  is the foot of perpendicular from  $S$  onto  $TI_A$  then  $P\in\odot(AMN)$ . Now notice that  $M$  is the Orthocenter of  $\triangle TDS$ , so by Brocard's Theorem we get that  $\overline{P-D-L_!}$ . Now  $TD\cdot TK=TA\cdot TS=TI\cdot TL_1\implies L_1\in\odot(IDK)$ . So,  $\odot(AMN)\cap\odot(KID)=L_1$ . Now let  $TL_1\cap\odot(ABC)=Y\implies MY\perp TL_1$  also  $MN\perp TL_1\implies\overline{M-Y-N}$ . Now by a Homothety at  $H$  with scale factor of  $1/2$  we get that  $L_1\mapsto Y\implies$  Midpoint of  $IL_1$  is  $Y\in\odot(ABC)$ .  $\blacksquare$

