Let  $L$  be the midpoint of arc  $BAC$ ,  $T$  be the  $A$ -mixtilinear intouch point on  $\Omega$ ,  $E$  be the foot of the altitude from  $I$  to  $\overline{BC}$ , and  $I'$  be the reflection of  $I$  over  $T$ . It suffices to show that  $I'$  lies on both  $(KID)$  and  $(MAN)$ .**Key Claim:**  $M$ ,  $T$ ,  $N$  are collinear. 

*Proof.* WLOG assume  $AB<AC$  and let  $\theta = \tfrac{\angle A}{2} + \angle C = \angle ADS = \angle ALM$ . It is well known that  $TEDM$  cyclic; let this circle be  $\omega$ . Define a function  $f: \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$  such that for any point  $P$    $$ f(P) = \text{Pow}(P,\omega) - \text{Pow}(P,\Omega). $$   It is well known that  $f$  is linear. Thus \begin{align*} 2f(N) &= f(I) + f(S)  &= [(ID \cdot IM) - (-AI \cdot IM)] + [(SE \cdot SD) - (SA \cdot SL)]  &= IM(ID+AI) + SE \cdot (AD \sec \theta) - (AD \tan \theta) \cdot SL  &= (AD \sec \theta)[IM \cos \theta + SE - SL \sin \theta]  &= (AD \sec \theta)[\mathrm{dis}(I,\overline{LM}) + SE - \mathrm{dis}(S,\overline{LM})]  &= 0, \end{align*} so  $f(N) = 0$  and  $N$  lies on the radical axis  $\overline{TM}$  as desired.  $\square$ **Claim:**  $I' \in (MAN)$ .

*Proof.* It follows by our previous claim and the well-known fact that  $T \in \overline{IL}$  that  $\overline{NM} \perp \overline{LI}$ . Thus by homothety at  $I$  we have  $I'$  is the foot of the altitude from  $S$  to  $\overline{IL}$  and  $M$  is the midpoint of  $II_A$  where the  $A$ -excenter  $I_A$  is the orthocenter of  $\triangle ISL$ . We may conclude since  $M$ ,  $A$ ,  $N$ ,  $I'$  all lie on the nine-point circle of  $\triangle ISL$ .  $\square$ **Claim:**  $I' \in (KID)$ .

*Proof.* Note that by our previous results we have  $SLKI'$ ,  $SADK$  cyclic with diameters  $\overline{SL}$ ,  $\overline{SD}$  respectively. Then   $$ \measuredangle II'K = \measuredangle LI'K = \measuredangle LSK = \measuredangle ASK = \measuredangle ADK = \measuredangle IDK $$   and the conclusion follows.  $\square$  $\blacksquare$

