Let  $W$  and  $X$  be the midpoints of segment  $BC$  and arc  $BAC$  respectively. Let  $I_A$  be the  $A$  - excenter. Notice that  $S$  is the orthocenter of  $\triangle XDM$ , so  $\overline{AX}$  also passes through  $S$ . Since  $MW\cdot MX = MI^2=MI_A^2$  , we see that  $W$  is the  $X$  - Humpty point of  $\triangle XII_A$ . This means that the orthocenter of this triangle lies on the line through  $W$  perpendicular to  $\overline{XM}$ . Since it must also lie on  $\overline{XA}$ , it follows that  $S$  is in fact the orthocenter of  $\triangle XII_A$  . Now let  $L=\overline{XI}\cap \overline{SI_A}$  , and let  $T$  be the midpoint of segment  $IL$ . Since  $(MAN)$  is the nine point circle of  $\triangle XSI_A$  , it passes through  $L$ . Moreover,  $L$  lies on  $(BIC)$  as  $\angle ILI_A=90^\circ$ . Therefore, 
\[XD\cdot XK = XW\cdot XM = XB^2 = XI\cdot XL,\]
which shows that  $L$  lies on  $(KID)$  as well. Now since  $MT\parallel I_AL$  , it follows that  $\angle XTM=90^\circ$  so  $T$  lies on  $\Omega$  as desired.
