i) Each pair of unit squares which are symmetry by  $AC$  are labelled with the same integer from the closed interval  $[-k,k]$ ii) If a row and a column intersectes at a square that is colored by black, then the set of positive integers on that row and the set of positive integers on that column are distinct.If a row and a column intersectes at a square that is colored by white, then the set of negative integers on that row and the set of negative integers on that column are distinct.

