Let  $\theta = \angle I_1AX$ . Note that by the Law of Sines on  $\triangle ABX$  and  $\triangle ACX$ , 
\begin{align*}
AI_1 &= \frac{AB \sin \frac B2}{\sin\left(\theta+\frac B2\right)} 
AI_2 &= \frac{AC \sin \frac C2}{\sin\left(\frac A2 - \theta + \frac C2\right)} = \frac{AC \sin \frac C2}{\cos\left(\frac B2+\theta\right)}.
\end{align*}
So the sine area formula yields 
\begin{align*}
[AI_1I_2] &= \frac 12 \cdot AI_1 \cdot AI_2 \cdot \sin \frac A2  
&= \frac 12 \cdot \frac{AB \sin \frac B2 AC \sin \frac C2 \sin \frac A2}{\sin\left(\theta + \frac B2\right)\cos \left(\theta + \frac B2\right)} 
&\geq \frac 12 \cdot \frac{bc \sin \frac A2 \sin \frac B2 \sin \frac C2}{\frac 12} 
&\geq \frac{bc(-a+b+c)(a-b+c)(a+b-c)}{8abc} 
&\geq \boxed{126}
\end{align*}
by using the well-known identities for sine half-angle.

I really liked this, solved it in  $5$  minutes!
