Now we induct on  $k$  to show the upper bound and an additional statement: In any optimal coloring, all cells in the bottom row and the rightmost column must not all be the same color. Base case  $k=1$  is some casework. 

Inductive step: Consider the following two "shells" (call red one the first shell and blue one the second shell) and label the three corners of the first shell  $A,B,C$  as shown. 
[asy]
size(4cm);
