Each of the shaded cells will be connected to at least one component from the first shell, so we won't count it. Any two adjacent cells can contribute at most 1 to  $M$  (If two cells have the same color, we are done. Otherwise, at least one of them shares the same color as the cell adjacent to both of them in the first shell). Hence, the blue part contributes at most  $\frac{n-1}{2}$  to  $M$  so  $M\le\frac{n-1}{2}$ . Note that  $M$  is an integer to get the desired result.</details> $G$  is of type 2.1 (containing  $A$  or  $C$ ):  $M\le \left\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\right\rfloor$ <details><summary>Proof</summary>[asy]
