We now go by induction on  $n$ . Let  $S_n$  be the working set for  $n$  and let  $2T$  be the total of all the elements in  $S_n$ . Then define  $A_k \subset S_n$  to be the subset of size  $2 \leq k \leq n$  with total  $T$ . We define:  $$ S_{n+2}=S_n \cup \{T,2T,3T,4T\} $$  This has  $2n+4$  elements as  $S_n$  cannot contain an element  $\geq T$  by considering  $A_2$  and  $S_n \setminus A_2$  which both have total of elements  $T$  and neither can contain an element  $\geq T$ .

