Recall that  $\ell \equiv \overline{HD}$  is the reflection of line  $\overline{APT}$  across  $x$ . As  $\overline{HP} \parallel \overline{AD}$ ,  $x$  is also the perpendicular bisector of  $\overline{PH}$ . Similarly,  $y$  and  $z$  are the perpendicular bisectors of  $\overline{QH}$  and  $\overline{RH}$ . Since  $H$  is the incenter of  $\triangle PQR$ , this implies that our perpendicular bisectors determine a triangle with circumcircle  $\gamma$ , as the meet at the arc midpoints of  $\gamma$ . This is the desired result.**<span style="color:red">Remark:</span>**  	For me, most of the difficulty in this solution is identifying all 	the relevant points  $T$ ,  $P$ ,  $Q$ ,  $R$ ,  $H$ , 	which can be found from an accurately drawn diagram.

