<details><summary>Solution</summary>Let  $M$  be the midpoint of  $OP$ . It is clear that  $O_A,O_B,O_C$  all lie on the perpendicular bisector of  $OP$ . Let the intersections  $\ell_B\cap \ell_C,\ell_C\cap\ell_A$  and  $\ell_A\cap\ell_B$  be denoted by  $X,Y,Z$  respectively.
