<details><summary>Complex</summary>Since the perpendicular bisectors of  $B_1T$  and  $C_1T$  meet at  $A$ ,  $A$  is the circumcenter of  $(B_1C_1T)$ . Restate the problem as follows:
<blockquote>
Let  $\Omega$  be a circle. Choose points  $A_1,B_1,C_1,A_2,B_2,C_2$  such that  $A_1A_2, B_1B_2, C_1C_2$  concur. Call this concurrency point  $T$ . Let  $A$  be the circumcenter of  $(B_1C_1T)$ , and define  $B,C$  similarly. Prove  $AA_2, BB_2, CC_2$  meet on  $\Omega$ . 
</blockquote>
We use complex numbers, with  $(A_1B_1C_1)$  as the unit circle. Let  $A_1=a_1, B_1=b_1, C_1=c_1$ , and  $A_2=a_2, B_2=b_2, C_2=c_2$ , and  $T=t$ . We know  $T \in A_1A_2, T\in B_1B_2, T\in C_1C_2$ . So
\begin{align*}
a_1+a_2 &= t + a_1a_2 \overline{t} \implies a_2 = \frac{t-a_1}{1-a_1\overline{t}} 
\end{align*}
By the circumcenter formula, 
\begin{align*} 
a &= \frac{\begin{vmatrix} b_1 & 1 & 1  c_1 & 1 & 1  t & t\overline{t} & 1 \end{vmatrix}}{\begin{vmatrix} b_1 & 1/b_1 & 1  c_1 & 1/c_1 & 1  t & \overline{t} & 1 \end{vmatrix}} 
&= \frac{(b_1-c_1)(1-t\overline{t})}{b_1(1/c_1 - \overline{t}) - c_1(1/b_1-\overline{t}) + t(1/b_1-1/c_1)} 
&= \frac{(b_1-c_1)(1-t\overline{t})}{(b_1-c_1)\left( \frac{1}{b_1} + \frac{1}{c_1} - \overline{t} - \frac{t}{b_1c_1}\right)} 
&= \frac{b_1c_1(1-t\overline{t})}{b_1+c_1-b_1c_1\overline{t} - t}.
\end{align*}
Now note
\[ \overline{a} = \frac{\frac{1}{b_1c_1}\left(1-t\overline{t} \right)}{\frac{1}{b_1} + \frac{1}{c_1} - \frac{t}{b_1c_1} - \overline{t}} = \frac{1-t\overline{t}}{b_1+c_1 - b_1c_1\overline{t} - t} = \frac{a}{b_1c_1}. \]
Now we have to verify that  $AA_2 \cap \Omega$  is symmetric in  $a_1,b_1,c_1$ . Let  $X=AA_2 \cap \Omega$ , (so  $x$  lies on the unit circle). Since  $A$  lies on chord  $A_2X$  of the unit circle,
\begin{align*}
a_2+x = a+a_2x \overline{a} &\implies x = \frac{a-a_2}{1-a_2\overline{a}}. 
\end{align*}
So
\begin{align*}
x &= \frac{a-a_2}{1-a_2\overline{a}} 
&= \frac{\frac{b_1c_1(1-t\overline{t})}{b_1+c_1-b_1c_1\overline{t} - t} - \frac{t-a_1}{1-a_1\overline{t}}}{1- \frac{t-a_1}{1-a_1\overline{t}} \cdot \frac{1-t\overline{t}}{b_1+c_1 - b_1c_1\overline{t} - t} } 
&= \frac{b_1c_1(1-t\overline{t})(1-a_1\overline{t}) - (t-a_1)(b_1+c_1 - b_1c_1\overline{t}-t)}{(1-a_1\overline{t})(b_1+c_1-b_1c_1\overline{t}-t) - (t-a_1)(1-t\overline{t})} 
&= \frac{b_1c_1(1-a_1\overline{t}-t\overline{t} + a_1t\overline{t}^2) - (tb_1+tc_1-b_1c_1t\overline{t} - t^2 - a_1b_1-a_1c_1 + a_1b_1c_1\overline{t} + a_1t)}{(b_1+c_1-b_1c_1\overline{t}-t - a_1b_1\overline{t}-a_1c_1\overline{t}+a_1b_1c_1 \overline{t}^2 + a_1t\overline{t}) - (t-t^2\overline{t} - a_1+a_1t\overline{t})} 
&= \frac{(b_1c_1 + c_1a_1+a_1b_1) + a_1b_1c_1t\overline{t}^2 - t(a_1+b_1+c_1) - t^2}{(a_1+b_1+c_1) - (a_1b_1+b_1c_1+c_1a_1)\overline{t} - 2t  + a_1b_1c_1 \overline{t}^2  + t^2\overline{t}}
\end{align*}
which is clearly symmetric in  $a_1,b_1,c_1$ .</details>

