Let  $\angle BAP = \angle IAQ = \theta$ ; it is easy to see that these two angles are equal. Then 
\begin{align*}
\frac{AB \sin \theta}{IA \sin\left(\frac A2-\theta\right)} &= \frac{BP}{PI} = \frac{ID \sin \alpha}{ID \cos \alpha} 
\frac{IA \sin \theta}{AC \sin\left(\frac A2-\theta\right)} &= \frac{IQ}{QC} = \frac{ID \sin \beta}{CD \cos \beta}
\end{align*}
by the ratio lemma. Dividing the two expressions,   $$ \frac{AB \cdot AC}{IA^2} = \frac{BD \cdot CD}{ID^2} \cdot \frac{\tan \alpha}{\tan \beta}. $$   So it suffices to show that   $$ \frac{AB \cdot AC}{IA^2} = \frac{\cos \frac C2 \cos \frac B2}{\sin \frac B2 \sin \frac C2} = \cot \frac B2 \cot \frac C2 = \frac{BD \cdot CD}{ID^2}, $$   which is obviously true.

