Consider  $\triangle LDF$  and  $\triangle LDE$ . We have  $ED=DF$  and  $\angle ADE=\angle ADF$  which gives  $\triangle LDF\cong \triangle LDE$ . So,  $LE=LF$ . So we have  $LC=LF=LE$  which gives  $\triangle CEL$  is isosceles.

