Proof:  $\angle BFE = \angle BFC + \angle CFE = (180^{\circ}- 60^{\circ}) + \angle CDE = 180^{\circ}$ . So,  $F$  lies on  $BE$ . Similarly  $\angle AFD=\angle AFC+\angle CFD=\angle ABC+(180^{\circ}-60^{\circ})=180^{\circ}$ . So  $F$  lies on  $AD$  which gives us that  $F$  is the intersection of  $AD$  and  $BE$ .

Claim 2:  $\triangle CFK$  is equilateral.

