So we need, \[AH+CH-AC=2BH-AB-BC+AC=AB-AC-BH+CH.\]

Replace  $AH=AB-BH$ , we need  $AB-BH+CH-AC=AB-AC-BH+CH$  which is true.

Now we need  $AH+CH-AC=2BH-AB-BC+AC$ . So, we need  $AH+CH=2BH-AB-BC+2AC=2BH-AB=BH-AH$  or  $2AH+CH=BH$ .

So we need  $2\cdot \frac{AH}{CH}+1=\frac{BH}{CH}$ . Now from similarity,  $\frac{AH}{CH}=\frac{AC}{BC}=\frac{1}{2}$  and  $\frac{BH}{CH}=\frac{BC}{AC}=2$ . $2\cdot \frac{AH}{CH}+1=2=\frac{BH}{CH}$ . 

Proved.

